{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-2","kind":"proposition","title":"辗转相减不停机与不可公度","englishTitle":"If, when the less of two unequal magnitudes is continually subtracted in turn from the greater, that which is left never measures the one before it, the magnitudes will be incommensurable.","book":10,"number":2,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.2","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.2/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":2,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","contentId":"euclid-10-2","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"10b9d8cc0fe80126bd53df3ba35b4e511f157e92eea0e1e9220cc479f161e024","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-2.statement","euclid-10-2.proof.1","euclid-10-2.proof.2","euclid-10-2.construction.1","euclid-10-2.proof.3","euclid-10-2.proof.4","euclid-10-2.proof.5","euclid-10-2.proof.6","euclid-10-2.proof.7","euclid-10-2.proof.8","euclid-10-2.conclusion","euclid-10-2.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-2.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d0146ceae886df1320834cde2d6438e7a1d57d4e7d8e79835cedb058ccd47627","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If, when the less of two unequal magnitudes is continually subtracted in turn from the greater, that which is left never measures the one before it, the magnitudes will be incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果两个不平等的音量的较小数量从较大数量中不断减去,而剩下的也从未测量到它面前的音量,那么,音量将达到不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":1,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"bc27e80d424bdd729f65a6db620812157cd6e38522db9f2ef44409cf69b67150","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, there being two unequal magnitudes AB, CD, and AB being the less, when the less is continually subtracted in turn from the greater, let that which is left over never measure the one before it; I say that the magnitudes AB, CD are incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,有两种不平等的数值,即AB、CD和AB,数量较小,而较少的数量则从较大数量中不断减去,而剩下的数量永远不能计量;我说,AB、CD等值是不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8a8bf44468cbd411d245e0a388bb31c9f690039cccf7dd0145be4d971a9f2a80","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if they are commensurable, some magnitude will measure them."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,如果它们是可公度, 一定能测量它们。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":3,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"dff498790aded2a28617b65ce5472a2548a58376fdb5406352caf9b09c543e42","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let a magnitude measure them, if possible, and let it be E; let AB, measuring FD, leave CF less than itself, let CF measuring BG, leave AG less than itself, and let this process be repeated continually, until there is left some magnitude which is less than E."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能的话,让我们用一个数量来衡量它们,让它达到E;让AB, FD, CF, BG, BG, AG, 并且让这一进程不断重复,直到还剩下不到E的某个数量。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8afae4a534eb37ee04ea8ce0737ea86c9e4a23397520b18a16105e20c12a46d1","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Suppose this done, and let there be left AG less than E."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果这样的话,就让AG少一点"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"45a5a8c6e39841dcd2f84f7fbb02864b79787f05639079fc7c5598ba43ae1e00","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Then, since E measures AB, while AB measures DF, therefore E will also measure FD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"其后,自E项措施AB项措施以来,AB项措施DF项措施,因此,E项措施也将是FD项措施。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"fe8c8b02e19860b37736c8a80d89203daf1f1cd898b84da883761cd761375202","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures the whole CD also; therefore it will also measure the remainder CF."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但它也衡量整个CD;因此,它也将衡量其余的CF。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b3317d968a04930be280a22747ec3177a06c683fc127cb8be513b5c77b74291b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But CF measures BG; therefore E also measures BG."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但CF项措施为BG项,因此E项措施为BG项。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"afe61e2f30b2c92b9d926306118a689adf2ff4fc9ad3b3956e66cbbc98a0fc13","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures the whole AB also; therefore it will also measure the remainder AG, the greater the less: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但它也测量了整个AB;因此,它也将测量其余的AG,数量越大,数量就越小:这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"2dbd841b016fb1877bff79a93c0b48a31f0109338f2de5ef458e2f8980d27754","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore no magnitude will measure the magnitudes AB, CD; therefore the magnitudes AB, CD are incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,任何数值都无法测量AB,CD;因此,AB,CD是不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":10,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"3229e4471609b16a294eaaf297973f1853830348c8e2781609e85a40cf99f643","citations":["euclid-10-def-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. [[X. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-10-def-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由此命题得证。 [[X. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-10-def-1)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-2.source","contentId":"euclid-10-2","revisionId":"euclid-10-2@raw-10b9d8cc0fe80126","order":11,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8ca1f8cf71c75d539e791bbe727e65d98bafc80429bae4fafaf5f6b139a7403a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.2/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.2\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-2:euclid-10-def-1:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-2","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-2.conclusion"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-def-1","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.2","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.2/","sourceLabel":"X. Def. 1"}}],"incomingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-3:euclid-10-2:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-3.proof.5"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-2","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3/","sourceLabel":"X. 2"}}],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-10-2:euclid-10-def-1:explicit","id":"euclid-10-def-1","book":10,"number":1,"kind":"definition","title":"可公度量与不可公度量","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-10-3:euclid-10-2:explicit","id":"euclid-10-3","book":10,"number":3,"kind":"proposition","title":"求两个可公度量的最大公度","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-irrational","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
